            <li><strong>Disability Care:</strong> Awareness events and comprehensive support, such as the Inclusive Horseback Ride with future physical therapists, which reinforces emotional and social support for people with disabilities and their families.</li>
            <li><strong>Applied Research:</strong> Project featured at international congress co-designing Universal Communicative Accessibility solutions with people with visual, physical, and hearing disabilities in Valledupar. Research from the Physical Therapy program on barriers to inclusion of students with disabilities won first place at a regional symposium.</li>
            <li><strong>Training Leaders for Peace:</strong> Alliance with the University for Peace (UPEACE) to train leaders with a focus on integral human development, peaceful transformation of conflicts, sustainable development, with elements of gender equity and non-discrimination, including themes on the fight against poverty.</li>
