  <div class="hero">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow" data-lang-content data-lang="es" data-visible="true">Objetivos de Desarrollo Sostenible</div>
        <div class="eyebrow" data-lang-content data-lang="en">Sustainable Development Goals</div>
  <h1 data-lang-content data-lang="es">ODS 5: Igualdad de Género</h1>
  <h1 data-lang-content data-lang="en">SDG 5: Gender Equality</h1>
  <p style="margin-top: 24px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); text-align: justify;" data-lang-content data-lang="es">El Objetivo de Desarrollo Sostenible 5 (ODS 5) busca "lograr la igualdad entre los géneros y empoderar a todas las mujeres y las niñas", eliminando la discriminación y la violencia.</p>
  <p style="margin-top: 24px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); text-align: justify;" data-lang-content data-lang="en">Sustainable Development Goal 5 (SDG 5) seeks to "achieve gender equality and empower all women and girls," eliminating discrimination and violence.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;">
  <img src="https://sdgbook.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2019/09/5.png" alt="Logo ODS 5" class="hero-illustration" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='https://placehold.co/320x320/FF3A21/ffffff?text=ODS+5';"/>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
    <!-- Sección: Inclusión con enfoque de género (añadida) -->
    <section id="inclusion-genero" style="background: var(--bg-white);">
      <div class="container">
      
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:12px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en">
            Our "Inclusion Policy" has a deliberate, gender-focused approach that produces tangible results. In 2024 we welcomed 16 new students who are the first in their families to access higher education. Each one represents the breaking of a cycle and the materialization of UDES as a true platform of social mobility for women in the region.
          </p>

        <!-- Indicadores (cifras) moved to a dedicated section below -->
          <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:12px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en">
            At the University of Santander, our commitment to gender equality goes beyond metrics; it is a daily practice reflected in our community, culture and academia. We not only recognize the value of the women who "make UDES great" on International Women's Day, but we actively promote their leadership, highlight entrepreneurial stories like that of artisan Janeth Viviescas, and create spaces for critical dialogue about the realities they face, as shown by the release of the documentary ‘Al final del silencio’. From the Nursing program to cultural events, we foster an environment where female talent takes center stage.
          </p>

          <!-- Cifras 2024 -->
          <div style="margin-top:8px; margin-bottom:12px;">
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:8px;" data-lang-content data-lang="es">La Universidad de Santander (UDES) es un agente activo en este propósito, utilizando su plataforma educativa, sus medios de comunicación y sus programas de extensión para fomentar la equidad, visibilizar el aporte femenino y combatir activamente la violencia de género.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:8px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en">The University of Santander (UDES) is an active agent in this purpose, using its educational platform, media and outreach programs to promote equity, highlight women's contributions and actively combat gender-based violence.</p>

            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:8px;" data-lang-content data-lang="es"><strong>Este compromiso se fundamenta en acciones concretas y se refleja en nuestras cifras de 2024:</strong></p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="es"><strong>Acceso y Oportunidad:</strong> Dimos la bienvenida a 16 nuevas estudiantes que, además de iniciar su carrera, son pioneras al ser la primera generación de sus familias en acceder a la educación superior.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="es"><strong>Liderazgo Académico:</strong> Nuestro cuerpo docente se fortalece con el talento de 5 ingenieras de alto nivel (Ingeniería Química, Industrial, Agroindustrial, de Producción y Mecánica), varias de ellas con títulos de maestría, quienes forman a las futuras generaciones con innovación y excelencia.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="es"><strong>Impacto Profesional (Campus Cúcuta):</strong> En 2024, celebramos la graduación de 522 mujeres que obtuvieron sus títulos profesionales en nuestros diversos programas.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="es"><strong>Avance en Áreas STEM:</strong> Demostrando la creciente participación femenina en campos estratégicos, 3 de los 12 nuevos graduados en programas STEM clave (como Ingeniería Industrial) fueron mujeres, representando un 25% de esa cohorte específica.</p>

            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-top:10px; margin-bottom:8px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en"><strong>This commitment is grounded in concrete actions and is reflected in our 2024 figures:</strong></p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en"><strong>Access & Opportunity:</strong> We welcomed 16 new students who, in addition to starting their studies, are pioneers as the first generation in their families to access higher education.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en"><strong>Academic Leadership:</strong> Our faculty is strengthened by the talent of five high-level female engineers (Chemical, Industrial, Agroindustrial, Production and Mechanical Engineering), several holding master's degrees, who train future generations with innovation and excellence.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en"><strong>Professional Impact (Cúcuta Campus):</strong> In 2024 we celebrated the graduation of 522 women who earned professional degrees across our programs.</p>
            <p style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-primary); text-align:justify; margin-bottom:6px;" data-lang-content data-lang="en"><strong>STEM Progress:</strong> Demonstrating growing female participation in strategic fields, 3 of the 12 new graduates in key STEM programs (such as Industrial Engineering) were women, representing 25% of that specific cohort.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

